# AJAX & CSRF Standards

## Backend (Controllers)
- All AJAX-only endpoints must validate the request:
  ```php
  if (!$this->request->isAJAX()) {
      throw \CodeIgniter\Exceptions\PageNotFoundException::forPageNotFound();
  }
  ```

## Frontend (JS/Fetch)
- **Headers**: Always include `X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest`.
- **CSRF Injection**: For mutative requests (POST, PUT, DELETE), inject the CSRF token in headers using `<?= csrf_header() ?>`.
- **CSRF Renewal**: Always capture the new token from the response header and update the global `#csrf_token` input.

## Views
- Include the CSRF hidden input at the start of the `main` section:
  ```html
  <input type="hidden" name="<?= csrf_token() ?>" value="<?= csrf_hash() ?>" id="csrf_token">
  ```

## DataTables
- Use `xhr.dt` event to renew the CSRF token:
  ```javascript
  $('#tabla').on('xhr.dt', function (e, settings, json, xhr) {
      if (xhr && xhr.getResponseHeader('<?= csrf_header() ?>')) {
          document.getElementById('csrf_token').value = xhr.getResponseHeader('<?= csrf_header() ?>');
      }
  });
  ```
